.SH "policy"
.PP
A policy nobody dares switch on is not a control, and the reason nobody dares is always the same: no one knows what it would refuse at three in the morning. Shadow mode is the answer the WAF has had for years, generalised to every protocol \[u2014] the policy is evaluated on real traffic, every decision it would have made is written down, and nothing is refused for policy.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
.ft CR
policy:
  mode: shadow          # enforce (default) or shadow
  max_reasons: 4096
.ft
.fi
.RE
.PP
.TS
