.SS "server.listeners[].tcp (kind: tcp)"
.PP
A \fBkind: tcp\fR listener forwards connections at layer 4. TLS connections are routed by the server name of the ClientHello, which is peeked and passed through unchanged, so the upstream terminates TLS with its own certificate and the client verifies that one. Connections that are not TLS, or whose name matches no route, go to \fBdefault\fR when set and are closed otherwise. A tcp listener takes no \fBtls\fR, \fBprotocols\fR, \fBh3\fR or \fBredirect_to_https\fR; bans and the global connection limits apply at accept as on every listener.
.PP
