.SS "server.listeners[].dns.dns64"
.PP
RFC 6147 address synthesis: an AAAA answer for a name that has only an A record, so an IPv6\-only client can reach an IPv4\-only service through a translator.
.PP
The client asks for AAAA, the name has none, and this resolver asks for A instead and answers with that IPv4 address embedded in a prefix (RFC 6052) routed to the translator. Nothing on the client changes \[u2014] it believes it is speaking IPv6 throughout, which is the point.
.PP
