\fB\fBauth\fR\fR is symmetric authentication. RFC 8573 makes AES\-CMAC the algorithm: the older construction is MD5 over the key followed by the packet, which is a length\-extension shape with a broken hash in it. The legacy algorithms are an explicit exception rather than a default, because a device from 2006 cannot be taught a new one and pretending otherwise ends with no authentication at all rather than weak authentication somebody knows about. \fBAutokey (RFC 5906) is not implemented and will not be\fR; its extension fields fall under the unknown\-field policy like anything else this relay cannot reason about.
.PP
.TS
