.SS "server.listeners[].ssh.principals"
.PP
Without this list a bastion has one policy for everyone in \fBauthorized_keys\fR: the deployment robot may run what the on\-call engineer may run. Each entry names who it covers and what they may do, and the listener\(aqs own settings are what an entry leaves unset \[u2014] so an entry that only moves someone to another account on the target says only that.
.PP
The list is the policy. Once there is one entry, a key no entry covers is refused at authentication rather than served under the listener\(aqs default, because falling back would be the opposite of what the list says.
.PP
.TS
