.PP
The OTLP exporter sends the same families as OTLP/HTTP with JSON encoding: counters as cumulative monotonic sums since process start, gauges as gauges, histograms as cumulative explicit bucket histograms; labels become data point attributes. \fBGET /v1/otlp\fR and \fBxproxyctl otlp\fR show pushes, failures, the last error and the size of the last request.
.PP
Exposed families: \fBxproxy_requests_total\fR, \fBxproxy_responses_total{class}\fR, \fBxproxy_denied_total{reason}\fR, \fBxproxy_refusals_total{kind,reason}\fR (the same breakdown for the protocols that are not HTTP: the listener kind that refused and the reason it logged, described in TROUBLESHOOTING.md), \fBxproxy_refusals_untracked_total\fR, \fBxproxy_bytes_in_total\fR, \fBxproxy_bytes_out_total\fR, \fBxproxy_waf_detected_total\fR, \fBxproxy_upstream_errors_total\fR, \fBxproxy_upstream_timeouts_total\fR, \fBxproxy_upstream_no_healthy_total\fR, \fBxproxy_client_aborts_total\fR, \fBxproxy_connections_rejected_total\fR, \fBxproxy_reloads_total{result}\fR, \fBxproxy_bans_total\fR, \fBxproxy_challenges_total{result}\fR (\fBissued\fR, \fBpassed\fR, \fBfailed\fR, \fBcaptcha_passed\fR), \fBxproxy_sensitive_findings_total{kind}\fR, \fBxproxy_sensitive_messages_total{direction,outcome}\fR, \fBxproxy_account_actions_total{class,action}\fR, \fBxproxy_account_events_total\fR, \fBxproxy_account_blocks_total\fR, \fBxproxy_account_campaigns_total\fR, \fBxproxy_account_disposable_total\fR, \fBxproxy_account_blocks_active\fR, \fBxproxy_log_sent_total{sink}\fR, \fBxproxy_log_dropped_total{sink}\fR, \fBxproxy_connections_open\fR, \fBxproxy_requests_in_flight\fR, \fBxproxy_bans_active\fR, \fBxproxy_sessions_live\fR, \fBxproxy_sessions_total\fR, \fBxproxy_sessions_closed_total{by}\fR, \fBxproxy_load_level\fR, \fBxproxy_upstream_latency_seconds\fR, \fBxproxy_shedding{class}\fR, \fBxproxy_cluster_peers\fR, \fBxproxy_cluster_peers_connected\fR, \fBxproxy_cluster_messages_total{direction,type}\fR, \fBxproxy_cluster_rejected_total\fR, \fBxproxy_request_duration_seconds\fR (histogram), \fBxproxy_upstream_ttfb_seconds\fR (histogram), \fBxproxy_upstream_endpoint_{healthy,ejected,active}{upstream,endpoint}\fR, \fBxproxy_upstream_endpoint_{requests,errors}_total{upstream,endpoint}\fR, \fBxproxy_route_requests_total{route,outcome}\fR, \fBxproxy_build_info\fR, \fBxproxy_uptime_seconds\fR, \fBxproxy_config_generation\fR, \fBxproxy_panics_total\fR (panics contained on a connection or datagram goroutine; zero in a healthy process, and anything else is a bug worth a report).
.PP
Series (per\-second rates for counters, current values for gauges): \fBrequests\fR, \fBresponses_2xx\fR, \fBresponses_4xx\fR, \fBresponses_5xx\fR, \fBdenied\fR, \fBshed\fR, \fBbytes_in\fR, \fBbytes_out\fR, \fBupstream_errors\fR, \fBopen_connections\fR, \fBin_flight\fR, \fBload_level\fR, \fBupstream_latency_ms\fR, \fBbans_active\fR, \fBcluster_connected\fR.
.SH "api_inventory"
.PP
Present means enabled. The proxy discovers the API surface it serves from traffic: every request of a proxied route (not redirects, static files or honeypots) is attributed to its host, method and path template, with first and last seen times, counts per status class, the kinds of credential clients present (\fBbearer\fR, \fBbasic\fR, \fBapi_key\fR, \fBcookie\fR, \fBclient_cert\fR, \fBnone\fR), request and response media types and the version segment of the path (\fBv1\fR, \fBv2\fR). Identifiers in the path (numbers, UUIDs, hashes, opaque tokens) fold into \fB*\fR, so \fB/users/42\fR and \fB/users/43\fR are one endpoint; on a route with an \fBopenapi\fR filter the description\(aqs own template is used and the filter says whether the operation is documented. \fBxproxyctl api\fR and \fBGET /v1/api\fR show:
.RS 3n
.PP
.ti -3n
\(bu
\fBshadow\fR APIs: traffic to a described route outside its description (an undocumented path or method), the endpoints nobody reviewed;
.PP
.ti -3n
\(bu
\fBzombie\fR APIs: documented operations without any traffic for \fBzombie_after\fR, or never since the inventory started, the endpoints nobody uses but everyone still maintains;
.PP
.ti -3n
\(bu
\fBsuperseded\fR versions: a \fBv1\fR still receiving traffic next to a \fBv2\fR of the same host, method and path;
.PP
.ti -3n
\(bu
the plain inventory, sorted by requests, with \fBversions\fR, \fBdocumented\fR and \fBundocumented\fR views;
.PP
.ti -3n
\(bu
any view as an OpenAPI 3.0 skeleton (\fBxproxyctl api undocumented \-openapi\fR, \fBGET /v1/api?view=undocumented&format=openapi\fR): one path item per observed template with named path parameters, the observed methods, request and response media types, response status classes, the credential kinds as security schemes, hosts as servers and an \fBx\-xproxy\fR extension with the traffic evidence; schemas and descriptions are left for the API team to complete, after which the file serves an \fBopenapi\fR filter.
.RE
.PP
.PP
