.SS "waf.profiles[].json_schemas[]"
.PP
A schema binds a JSON Schema document to request paths. A matching request\(aqs JSON body is buffered (bounded by \fBwaf.request_body_limit\fR, 413 above it), validated and then handed to the rules unchanged. In \fBblock\fR mode a violation is denied with 400, reason \fBwaf\fR, detail \fBjson_schema:<name>:<first problem>\fR and a JSON problem body listing up to twenty issues; in \fBdetect\fR mode it is logged (\fBwaf_schema\fR, \fBwaf_schema_issue\fR) and the request continues. The evaluator is the one the \fBopenapi\fR filter uses: types, enums, constants, string lengths, patterns and formats, numeric bounds, array and object bounds, \fBproperties\fR, \fBpatternProperties\fR, \fBadditionalProperties\fR, \fBallOf\fR, \fBanyOf\fR, \fBoneOf\fR, \fBnot\fR and local \fB$ref\fR.
.PP
