.SS "routes[].mirror"
.PP
A mirrored route sends a copy of each request (sampled by \fBpercent\fR) to another upstream in the background while the live request proceeds as usual. The copy is built like the live outbound request (path rules, \fBhost_header\fR, forwarding headers, \fBrequest_headers\fR) and carries \fBX\-Xproxy\-Mirror: 1\fR and the same \fBX\-Request\-Id\fR; its response is read and discarded, so a slow, failing or absent mirror never changes what the client sees. Bodies are buffered up to \fBmax_body_bytes\fR so that both requests can read them; larger requests are proxied and not mirrored. Upgrade requests are never mirrored. Only routes with an \fBupstream\fR can mirror.
.PP
.TS
