T}
.TE
.PP
\fBhost_cidrs\fR is the selector for a host a finder reached by address because no name points at it \[u2014] a parked address, a range a provider assigned, a machine found in a range scan. It matches the \fBHost\fR header read as an address, in either family and in either spelling (\fB::ffff:198.51.100.7\fR is the IPv4 address it carries), and it never matches a name: the proxy does not resolve the \fBHost\fR header, and a document that turned on what a name resolves to would be answering on the client\(aqs word.
.PP
