A refusal\(aqs detail names the rule: \fBxml_doctype\fR, \fBxml_entity\fR, \fBxml_cdata\fR, \fBxml_comment\fR, \fBxml_processing_instruction\fR, \fBxml_size\fR, \fBxml_depth\fR, \fBxml_elements\fR, \fBxml_attributes\fR, \fBxml_name_length\fR, \fBxml_text_length\fR, \fBxml_encoding\fR, \fBxml_root\fR, \fBxml_element\fR or \fBxml_malformed\fR. The body is read whole and replayed byte for byte, so the application receives exactly what the client sent.
.PP
A SOAP endpoint, which is the common case:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
.ft CR
filters:
  \- name: soap
    kind: xml_guard
    options:
      content_types: [application/soap+xml, text/xml]
      require_root: Envelope
      require_root_namespace: http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/
      max_bytes: 262144
      max_depth: 32
      allow_processing_instructions: false
.ft
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBSchema validation is deliberately not implemented.\fR XSD is a language with its own parser, its own imports and its own denial\-of\-service history; a gateway that fetched and interpreted one would add a larger attack surface than it removed, and the application already has the schema. \fBrequire_root\fR, \fBrequire_root_namespace\fR, \fBallow_elements\fR and \fBdeny_elements\fR are a positive model of the document\(aqs shape without a schema language in the middle \[u2014] the same trade the positive security policy makes for the rest of a request. A malformed document is refused rather than forwarded, because two parsers disagree about what a malformed document means and that disagreement is where the interesting bugs live.
.SS "Kind \fBwasm\fR"
.PP
Runs a WebAssembly module per request in a sandbox. The module follows the ABI in EXTENDING.md (exports \fBxproxy_abi_version\fR, \fBxproxy_alloc\fR, \fBxproxy_on_request\fR, optionally \fBxproxy_on_response\fR; imports \fBget\fR, \fBset_header\fR, \fBremove_header\fR, \fBdeny\fR, \fBlog\fR, \fBlog_attr\fR from module \fBxproxy\fR). It is read and compiled at load and on reload; a broken module or a wrong ABI version is a load error.
.PP
.TS
