The compiler emits machine code into executable memory,\: which the shipped systemd unit (\fBMemoryDenyWriteExecute=\:yes\fR) and the macOS hardened runtime refuse;\: \fBauto\fR probes once per process and falls back to the interpreter,\: which needs no executable pages and is several times slower per call
T}
