\fBbody_\:limit\fR
T}	T{
int
T}	T{
\fB65536\fR
T}	T{
Bytes of a request or response body a module may read or set;\: a larger body is not exposed and streams through;\: 0 disables body access;\: at most 16 MiB
T}
.TE
.PP
Denies carry the status, reason and detail the module set with \fBdeny\fR; \fBlog_attr\fR values appear in the access log as \fBwasm_<key>\fR.
.SS "Kind \fBbot_score\fR"
.PP
Scores each request as automation from the user agent, the headers a browser always sends, the TLS fingerprint of the connection (JA3 and JA4, computed from the ClientHello) and the client\(aqs recent behaviour, then logs, challenges or denies by threshold.
.PP
.TS
allbox;
