list
T}	T{
any
T}	T{
Which roles a connection may \fIclaim\fR. It is a claim,\: not a credential \-\- the server decides \-\- so this says which attempts may be made,\: which is smaller and still useful: an estate where nothing should ever connect as \fBpostgres\fR can say so and have it hold before a password is guessed at
T}
T{
\fBallow_\:databases\fR,\: \fBdeny_\:databases\fR
T}	T{
list
T}	T{
any
T}	T{
Same,\: for the database. Absent in the startup packet it defaults to the user name,\: and the policy applies that default
T}
